    "updated_at": "2026-11-12T09:57:19Z",
    "body": "Integration with #1144 (#1139 wire-iso post + #534 wire verify) pushed: `5c49075a` merges `issue/534-wire-verify` (no textual conflicts) and `0d82d2e7` adds `feat(edm): wire verify and the wire-iso post read an open run as open`.\n\n- **Verify:** an open run (`left|right`) is judged by the kerf law against the part, so a kerf that touches the part blocks the post. The start-hole and slug laws are skipped, and the report line gives the reason. Both ends must stand clear of the stock by the kerf offset.\n- **Post:** `wire-iso.cps` threads at the run-in point and cuts the wire at the run-out point. It writes only the path's moves, so there is no return move. The closed punch golden is byte-identical.\n- **New tests:** `wire_post::an_open_cutoff_posts_its_golden_and_a_gouging_one_is_refused` (new golden `nc/wire-iso/wire_contour_open_cutoff.nc`) and `sim verify::wire::tests::an_open_run_is_judged_by_its_kerf_with_no_start_hole_or_slug`.\n- **Gate:** quick `--base origin/issue/534-wire-verify` on `0d82d2e7` is green (13.7 min, all app suites); clippy `-D warnings` on motion/sim/app is clean.\n\nThe PR is now stacked on #1144.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
